# Patch-ID: P-TAB-001 (slice S5, adapter 1) — service events + favicon
# Area: tab.
# Rationale: provide a typed, generation-checked service-event seam without
#   editing tab/008's frozen event files; favicon completions carry decoded,
#   re-encoded PNG refs under IPC-CONTRACT sections 3 and 7.
# Last-Rebased: 2026-11-02 (Chromium 156.0.8078.74).
# Helper whitelist: favicon::ContentFaviconDriver via chrome's favicon utils;
#   audit: WebContentsUserData + Profile FaviconService, no TabInterface,
#   BrowserWindowInterface, Browser, TabFeatures or Views instantiation.
#   The existing keyed-service graph owns the helper's database dependency.
# Lifetime: adapter is WebContentsUserData, unhooks its driver observer in
#   WebContentsDestroyed before user-data deletion; no deferred-id cleanup.
#   Captured content generations are checked, never restamped at completion.
# Cache: immutable random refs scoped to the addressed tab/profile, at most
#   16 entries of <=64 KiB, encode input <=256x256; clear on primary-page
#   change/no icon/encode failure/teardown. Refreshes with unchanged icon URLs
#   are processed. Retrieval respects max_blob_bytes and returns too_large.
# Drift: bounded cache eviction invalidates old refs (not_found); oversized
#   observer images clear the presentation instead of emitting an empty ref.
#   Service events remain typed scaffolding, with no wire transport yet.
# Additive files + an isolated mac :core sources block; existing bridge files
#   remain untouched. AttachFaviconAdapter is dormant until integration.
# Gate: build-p10 green attempt 1; final build-p11 green attempt 2 after
#   teardown guards/formatting, no compile failures. nm symbols + --version
#   156.0.8078.74 verified. G1-G5 PASS on final build (G3: grep -qa).
